\section{Detritus production}{


The rate \eqn{p_D} at which detritus biomass is produced by the
ecosystem has contributions from three sources:

\deqn{p_D = p_{D.f} + p_{D.d} + p_{D.ext}}{
       p_D = p_{D.f} + p_{D.d} + p_{D.ext}}

\eqn{p_{D.f}} comes from the biomass that is consumed but not
assimilated and is given by:

\deqn{p_{D.f} = \sum_i(1-\alpha_i)\int (1-f_i(w))\,E_i(w)\,N_i(w)\,dw}{
       p_{D.f} = \sum_i(1-\alpha_i)\int (1-f_i(w))\,E_i(w)\,N_i(w)\,dw}

where \eqn{f_i(w)} is the feeding level (see \code{\link[=algae_consumption]{algae_consumption()}}'s
"Algae consumption" section for how \code{satiation} controls it), so that
\eqn{(1-f_i(w))\,E_i(w)} is the biomass actually consumed (as opposed to
merely encountered) -- unlike algae consumption, which deliberately
ignores feeding level (see \code{\link[=algae_consumption]{algae_consumption()}}), detritus's egestion
term uses the same feeding-level-adjusted consumption rate as
\code{\link[=getDetritusConsumption]{getDetritusConsumption()}} and \code{\link[=detritus_consumption]{detritus_consumption()}}.

\eqn{p_{D.d}} comes from the biomass of fish that die, combining two
mortality sources that each decompose to detritus at their own rate:
senescence mortality (see \code{\link[=getSenMort]{getSenMort()}}) and external mortality, i.e.
local deaths that lead directly to detritus as well as deaths due to
predation by species that are not explicitly modelled, for example
transient predators, mammals, or sea birds. Only a proportion of each
source's dead biomass decomposes to detritus, set independently by
\code{sen_decomp} (senescence, default 0.8) and \code{ext_decomp} (external
mortality, default 0.2; see \code{\link[=setDetritusParams]{setDetritusParams()}}). The detritus
production from decomposing dead organisms is given by:

\deqn{p_{D.d} = \mathtt{sen\_decomp}\,
                 \sum_i\int\mu_{seni.i}(w)N_i(w)w\,dw +
                 \mathtt{ext\_decomp}\,
                 \sum_i\int\mu_{nat.i}(w)N_i(w)w\,dw}{
     p_{D.d} = sen_decomp * \sum_i\int\mu_{seni.i}(w)N_i(w)w\,dw +
                 ext_decomp *
                 \sum_i\int\mu_{nat.i}(w)N_i(w)w\,dw}

